  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "To study this phenomenon in non-human animals, rodent versions of the PRL task have been developed 40 , 41 . While human and non-human versions of the task are conceptually similar and may yield comparable behavioral results, to our knowledge, a systematic cross-species comparison of behavioral, computational, and neurophysiological markers of cognitive flexibility has not been reported.",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study compares neurophysiological markers of cognitive flexibility between humans and rats using a probabilistic reversal learning task. It explicitly states the use of non-human animals (rats) to study the phenomenon and compares these results with human data, fulfilling the criteria for including whole-animal-in-vivo studies."
